<div class="main-title">Likutay Halachos &mdash; Choshen Mishpat II</div>
<div class="sub-title">Hilchos Apitropos [Laws of Guardianship]</div>

<div class="halacha-title">Halacha 2 &mdash; Part B (&sect;&sect;7&ndash;11)</div>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;7</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">matanos la&rsquo;evyonim</span> [gifts to the poor] that are given on Purim. This is the aspect of the tzedakah mentioned above, which is the aspect of voices &mdash; in order to give birth to the minds, etc., as above. And therefore Haman wanted to nullify this, and wanted to weigh ten thousand kikar of silver to nullify, G&ndash;d forbid, the shekalim of Israel &mdash; that is, to nullify the aspect of the voices mentioned above, which are revealed through the tzedakah of the shekalim of Israel.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;On the first of Adar, they announce regarding the shekalim&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Shekalim 1:1)</span> &mdash; <span class="key-term">&ldquo;they announce&rdquo; [mashmi&rsquo;in] specifically</span> &mdash; the aspect of voices, as above. And Haman wanted to nullify this. And therefore on Purim we give matanos la&rsquo;evyonim, to arouse the aspect of the voices mentioned above, in order to give birth to the minds, as above. And therefore there is a custom to fast the Fast of Esther, and also to collect the money of shekalim then &mdash; all for the sake of the aspect of the voices mentioned above, through which the minds are born and revealed and emerge from the aspect of sleep, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;8</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="key-term">&ldquo;A person is obligated to become intoxicated on Purim until he does not know the difference between &lsquo;cursed is Haman&rsquo; and &lsquo;blessed is Mordechai&rsquo;&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Megillah 7b)</span>. And this is the aspect of the supreme makifim mentioned above, where the knowledge and the free will are all one, and where everything is good, and where it is the aspect of &ldquo;not knowing,&rdquo; etc. &mdash; and it is impossible to grasp this intellect now.</p>

<p>And on Purim one must become intoxicated until one ascends and reaches there. And the essential intoxication of Purim is with wine. This is the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Wine enters, the secret comes out&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Sanhedrin 38a)</span>. For it is brought in the teaching mentioned above, on the verse: &ldquo;Nachamu, nachamu, says your G&ndash;d,&rdquo; that wine is for &ldquo;raising the voice&rdquo; [la&rsquo;arama kala] &mdash; see there. And this is the aspect of the wine-drinking of Purim &mdash; this is the aspect of the voices mentioned above, which are aroused through the wine, which is the aspect of &ldquo;raising the voice.&rdquo; And through this the minds are revealed, in the aspect of: &ldquo;Wine enters, the secret comes out.&rdquo; For <span class="key-term">yayin</span> [wine] is given in seventy letters &mdash; this is the aspect of the seventy cries mentioned above. And through them the secret emerges and is revealed &mdash; that is, the minds and the makifim that are grasped through the aspect of the wine of Purim, which is the aspect of the seventy cries mentioned above. And through them the secret emerges and is revealed &mdash; that is, the minds and the makifim &mdash; which had previously been in secret, in the aspect of concealment, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;9</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">seudas Purim</span> [the Purim feast]. For through holy eating, the da&rsquo;as is completed, as is explained elsewhere. And this is the essential intention of holy eating &mdash; to complete the da&rsquo;as and the mind through it, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The righteous eats to satisfy his soul&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Mishlai 13:25)</span>, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;And He will satiate in the brilliances [tzachtzachos] your soul&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 58:11)</span> &mdash; as is brought in the words of Rabbainu, of blessed memory, elsewhere. And the <span class="key-term">tzachtzachos</span> are the aspect of the makifim mentioned above, which are the aspect of the lights of the tzachtzachos, as is known. And through holy eating, one merits this.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the eating of <span class="key-term">Shabbos</span>, which is a great mitzvah. For on Shabbos the makifim mentioned above shine &mdash; which are the aspect of Attika &mdash; for Shabbos is the aspect of Attika Kadisha, Ra&rsquo;ava D&rsquo;Ra&rsquo;avin [the Will of Wills], as is known. And therefore, then it is a great mitzvah to eat, in order to receive through the eating of Shabbos the illumination of the makifim, in the aspect of: &ldquo;And He will satiate in the tzachtzachos your soul,&rdquo; in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Then you shall delight in Hashem&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Yeshayahu 58:14)</span>. And this is the aspect of seudas Purim. For on Purim the makifim mentioned above are revealed and shine, the aspect of Attika, the aspect of Mordechai, as above &mdash; the aspect of <span class="key-term">mor dror</span> [pure myrrh]. And it is taught in the Ra&rsquo;aya Mehemna: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Mekuteres mor&rdquo; &mdash; this is Keser</span> &mdash; which is the aspect of Attika, as is known. And therefore, on Purim it is a great mitzvah to eat, for then one receives through the eating the illumination of the supreme makifim mentioned above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;10</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">mishloach manos ish l&rsquo;rai&rsquo;aihu</span> [sending portions, each man to his fellow] &mdash; that is, each person must send to his fellow from the foods of Purim. This is the aspect of what Rabbainu, of blessed memory, wrote there in the teaching mentioned above: that one who merits the aspect of the revelation of the makifim &mdash; he must do good from his goodness to others and reveal the segulah to the am segulah. That is, to expound in public and reveal to others what he has merited that was revealed to him from the illumination of the makifim mentioned above, etc. &mdash; see there.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of mishloach manos ish l&rsquo;rai&rsquo;aihu. For the foods of Purim are the aspect of the illumination of the makifim. For in the holy foods &mdash; which are the aspect of the foods of Purim, as above &mdash; within them the minds and the makifim are revealed, as above. And therefore each person is obligated to send to his fellow from the foods of Purim &mdash; mishloach manos &mdash; in order to do good from his goodness to others. For the mishloach manos that one sends to his fellow from the foods of Purim &mdash; this alludes to the makifim that are merited on Purim, which shine within the foods, as above. Each person must reveal and illuminate in his fellow this illumination, and do good from his goodness to others, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore it is called <span class="key-term">mishloach manos</span> &mdash; from the word <span class="key-term">man</span> [manna]. For they are the aspect of the manna, which is da&rsquo;as, as is brought. The aspect of the food of the tzaddikim in the future, as our Sages of blessed memory said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Why are they called sh&rsquo;chakim? Because there they grind manna for the tzaddikim in the future&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Chagigah 12b)</span>. And the essential food of the tzaddikim in the future is the aspect of the attainment of the makifim mentioned above, which will be revealed in the future, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;The righteous will sit with their crowns on their heads&rdquo;</span> &mdash; as above. It emerges that the manna, which is the food of the tzaddikim in the future, is the aspect of da&rsquo;as, the aspect of the makifim mentioned above. And this is the aspect of the foods of Purim, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of mishloach manos &mdash; for they are the aspect of man [manna], which is the aspect of makifim, as above. And therefore each person must send to his fellow, in order to do good from his goodness to others, as above. For through eating, the neshamah is connected with the body, and the makif illuminates inward. For the body and neshamah are the aspect of p&rsquo;nimi and makif, as will be explained below. And therefore, through eating in holiness &mdash; the eating of Purim &mdash; through this specifically the makifim shine, as above. And from these makifim that are revealed on Purim, which are clothed within the foods, as above, each person sends to his fellow mishloach manos, as above.</p>

<div class="section-marker">&sect;11</div>

<p>And this is the aspect of the fact that we read <span class="key-term">Parshas Parah</span> [the Torah portion about the Red Heifer] after Purim. For the <span class="key-term">parah adumah</span> [Red Heifer] is a <span class="key-term">chukah</span> [statute beyond rational comprehension]. And this is the aspect of the makifim mentioned above, which are impossible to understand &mdash; which are the aspect of <span class="verse">&ldquo;the statute of the Torah&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Bamidbar 19:2)</span>, where it is impossible to understand the reason of the matter &mdash; such as the parah adumah, which renders the pure impure and purifies the impure.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of: &ldquo;A person is obligated to become intoxicated on Purim until he does not know the difference between &lsquo;cursed is Haman&rsquo; and &lsquo;blessed is Mordechai&rsquo;&rdquo; &mdash; this is the aspect of the makifim mentioned above that shine on Purim, as above. And therefore, after Purim, when the makifim mentioned above shine, as above, we then read Parshas Parah, which is also the aspect of the makifim mentioned above. For it is the statute of the Torah, which is impossible to understand, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the parah adumah, which is the aspect of the makifim mentioned above, purifies from <span class="key-term">tumas mais</span> [the impurity of death]. For through the illumination of the makifim mentioned above, through which the da&rsquo;as is completed, as above &mdash; through this one is purified from all impurities. As Rabbainu wrote there on the verse: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Create for me a pure heart, O G&ndash;d&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Tehillim 51:12)</span>, etc. &mdash; that the essential purification is through the movement of the intellect. For through the movement of the intellect, the flame of the heart rises of its own accord, and through this the heart is purified &mdash; see there in the teaching mentioned above and in the teaching that begins &ldquo;Laiv tahor b&rsquo;ra li Elokim&rdquo; <span class="inline-source">(siman 156)</span>, which also pertains to the teaching mentioned above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">burning of the parah</span> &mdash; the aspect of the flame of the heart, which is heated and kindled through the attainment of the makifim, through which the da&rsquo;as is completed. And all the makifim are drawn from the aspect of the supreme makifim, which are impossible to understand at all &mdash; which are the aspect of the parah adumah, the aspect of the statute of the Torah, as above.</p>

<p>For the essential impurity is tumas mais, and this is due to the departure of the neshamah, which is the light of the face [or hapanim], which is the aspect of the intellect. For the intellect is the neshamah that gives life to the body, in the aspect of: <span class="verse">&ldquo;Wisdom gives life&rdquo;</span> &mdash; and as is brought elsewhere. And when the neshamah, which is the intellect, departs, the body remains impure. For the essential purification is through the intellect, as above. (And this is the aspect of the seven days of mourning, G&ndash;d forbid, that are brought there in the teaching mentioned above &mdash; see there &mdash; in order to elevate the neshamah to the light of the face, since it has separated from the body &mdash; see there.)</p>

<p>For the body and the soul are the aspect of p&rsquo;nimi and makif. For the body is possible to understand through the intellect, but the neshamah is impossible to grasp. For the body and soul are the aspect of this world and the World to Come, the aspect of p&rsquo;nimi and makif. And the essential purification and sanctification of the body is through the intellect &mdash; the aspect of the neshamah, which is the aspect of the makifim mentioned above, which are the aspect of ruach hakodesh, which are the aspect of the purification of the heart, as above.</p>

<p>And therefore the parah adumah, which is the aspect of the makifim mentioned above, purifies from tumas mais. And therefore all the procedures of the parah are in sevens, as our Sages of blessed memory said: seven kohanim, seven washings, etc. This is the aspect of the seven lamps that are explained there, through which one draws the intellect from the light of the face mentioned above &mdash; see there.</p>

<p>For Adam HaRishon blemished the supreme makifim mentioned above, which are impossible to understand &mdash; and from this are drawn all the perplexities, such as the knowledge and the free will, as above. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">Eitz HaDa&rsquo;as Tov VaRa</span> [the Tree of Knowledge of Good and Evil] &mdash; that is, to know good and evil, which is the aspect of the free will &mdash; how it exists within the knowledge [of G&ndash;d]. And because he blemished this, it was said: <span class="verse">&ldquo;On the day you eat from it, you shall surely die&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Beraishis 2:17)</span>.</p>

<p>And therefore, through the parah adumah &mdash; the statute of the Torah, which purifies the impure and renders the pure impure &mdash; through this one purifies and nullifies tumas mais. Through believing in the aspect of the statute of the Torah &mdash; that is, in the supreme makifim mentioned above, which are impossible to understand &mdash; from this itself the makifim shine, and one merits that the illumination of the intellect is revealed to him &mdash; what it is possible for a human being to understand. And through this, the heart is purified, as above.</p>

<p>And this is the aspect of the parah adumah, all of whose procedures are in sevens &mdash; corresponding to the seven lamps mentioned above, through which the illumination of the intellect is drawn. And through this one is purified from all impurities. For the essential purification is through the movement of the intellect &mdash; see there.</p>

<p style="text-align:center; font-style:italic; color:#888; margin:20px 0;">Baruch Hashem l&rsquo;olam, Amain v&rsquo;Amain.</p>

<p><span class="verse">&ldquo;U&rsquo;mishloach manos ish l&rsquo;rai&rsquo;aihu u&rsquo;matanos la&rsquo;evyonim&rdquo;</span> <span class="inline-source">(Esther 9:22)</span> &mdash; the initial letters [of these words] spell <span class="key-term">Elul</span>. For Elul is the aspect of the attainment of the makifim, as is explained at the end of the teaching mentioned above. And understand this.</p>

<p class="end-marker">[End of Apitropos, Halacha 2]</p>

